{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BkWEDAqFyhMkq9u7MokNPP","type":"tool_result","content":"168:# The clip browser (rooms/clip_browser.toml; body = \"none\"): every [[npc]] whose name starts with\n169-# `cast` plays the same clip; pads step through the library, jump to a set's first clip or toggle\n170-# auto-play, and the clip's card lies on the floor at the object:\n171-#   behavior = { type = \"clip_browser\", next = \"clip_next\", back = \"clip_back\", auto = \"clip_auto\",\n172-#                cast = \"cast\", hold = 5, start = \"QUATERNIUS/Idle_Loop\",\n173-#                sets = [[\"clip_set_cmu\", \"CMU\"], [\"clip_set_quaternius\", \"QUATERNIUS\"]] }\n174-# An imported figure (a shipped pack's, e.g. LIB/kaykit_adventurers/knight) can wear any biped\n175:# [[npc]]: look = { figure = \"LIB/kaykit_adventurers/knight\" }.\n176-# More object fields: pitch = 20, roll = 0 (tilt in degrees, e.g. ramps), density = 1 (kg/m³:\n177-# 1 is very light; 50-100 = pushable crates; 400 = wood; 2000 = stone), friction = 0.5,\n178-# restitution = 0.0 (bounciness 0..1; rapier averages it with the surface underneath),\n179-# damping = 0 (air drag). Pushing shares momentum: a 70 kg character barely moves 300 kg.\n180-# Reusable props made in the Object Studio replace shape and colour:\n181-#   asset = \"BUILTIN/bench\", scale = 1, body = \"fixed\" (or \"none\": no collision),\n182-#   seed = 3 (a variant: chance, jitter and pick; 0 as authored),\n183-#   roles = { \"$wall\" = \"#5a6b7c\" } (colours for the theme roles its parts name),\n184-#   patch = [{ op = \"scale\", by = 0.5 }] (asset_edit patch ops on this copy only: a one-off\n185-#   variant, such as a defect on show in rooms/limits.toml; publish variants rooms reuse).\n186-#   `room_check` names any asset the library does not have, or a patch that does not apply.\n187-# Visual-only effects on any object (never affect the simulation; body = \"none\" for invisible\n--\n276:# [[npc]]\n277-# name = \"spidey\"\n278-# kind = \"spider\"\n279-# pos = [6.5, 0, 4.5]\n280-# ai = { type = \"wander\", radius = 3 }\n281-# look = { accent = \"#3bb273\", leg_length = 1.0 }\n105:# prop = { ..., sway = \"leaves\" }   props (and [[object]]s) can sway: \"leaves\" | \"grass\"\n106-#\n107-# zone = { kind = \"...\", ... } makes the tile a trigger (identical neighbours merge):\n108-#   kind = \"start\" | \"finish\" | \"gate\" | \"checkpoint\" | \"kill\" | \"water\" | \"pad\" | \"camera\" |\n109-#          \"conveyor\" (facing = direction, speed = m/s; carries characters and props) |\n110-#          \"bounce\" (speed = launch m/s; trampolines for characters and props)\n111-#   course = \"name\"   start/finish/gates of one course share it; leaving START starts the timer,\n112-#                     gates must be passed in `index` order (missed gate = +2 s), FINISH stops it\n113-#   index = 1         gate order\n--\n138:[[object]]\n139-name = \"ball\"\n140-shape = { type = \"sphere\", radius = 0.4 }\n141-pos = [3.5, 1.0, 3.5]           # x = column, y = height, z = row\n142-color = \"#5b8def\"\n143-body = \"dynamic\"                # dynamic | fixed | kinematic | none\n144-\n145-# Animated objects use body = \"kinematic\" and a behavior (vectors are in the object's own frame):\n146-#   behavior = { type = \"move\", offset = [0, 0, 4], period = 4, phase = 0, hold = 0.3, smooth = true }\n87:[layout.legend.'.']\n88-blocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0, color = \"#c8c8c8\" }]\n89-\n90:[layout.legend.'#']\n91-blocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0, color = \"#c8c8c8\" }, { y0 = 0, y1 = 2.0, color = \"#9aa5b1\" }]\n92-\n93:[layout.legend.'B']\n94-blocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0, color = \"#c8c8c8\" }, { y0 = 0, y1 = 1.0, color = \"#c9a27a\", rounded = true }]\n95-# Other options: destructible = true, ghost = true (no collision), inset = 0.3 (thinner),\n96-# crumble = 0.8 (falls 0.8 s after being stepped on), regrow = 4 (comes back after 4 s),\n97-# strength = 40 (breaks when hit with more than this contact force, e.g. glass),\n98-# look = \"flat\" | \"cel\" | \"lit\" | \"unlit\",\n99-# ladder = { facing = \"north\", height = 3.0 },\n100-# prop = { shape = { type = \"box\", half = [0.35, 0.35, 0.35] }, color = \"#e8704a\" },\n101-# marker = \"player\"\natrium.toml\ncabin.toml\ncorridor.toml\ndepot.toml\nnightward.toml\noffice.toml\nrecovery.toml\nscrub.toml\n[This command modified 2 files you've previously read: ../content.rs, ../field.rs. Call Read before editing.]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"189b0832-eeab-4401-af9a-06d1cd0033c9","uuid":"0d0eb1f2-29fe-4ecc-a3ed-630c577461a9","timestamp":"2026-11-05T14:46:28.457Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"168:# The clip browser (rooms/clip_browser.toml; body = \"none\"): every [[npc]] whose name starts with\n169-# `cast` plays the same clip; pads step through the library, jump to a set's first clip or toggle\n170-# auto-play, and the clip's card lies on the floor at the object:\n171-#   behavior = { type = \"clip_browser\", next = \"clip_next\", back = \"clip_back\", auto = \"clip_auto\",\n172-#                cast = \"cast\", hold = 5, start = \"QUATERNIUS/Idle_Loop\",\n173-#                sets = [[\"clip_set_cmu\", \"CMU\"], [\"clip_set_quaternius\", \"QUATERNIUS\"]] }\n174-# An imported figure (a shipped pack's, e.g. LIB/kaykit_adventurers/knight) can wear any biped\n175:# [[npc]]: look = { figure = \"LIB/kaykit_adventurers/knight\" }.\n176-# More object fields: pitch = 20, roll = 0 (tilt in degrees, e.g. ramps), density = 1 (kg/m³:\n177-# 1 is very light; 50-100 = pushable crates; 400 = wood; 2000 = stone), friction = 0.5,\n178-# restitution = 0.0 (bounciness 0..1; rapier averages it with the surface underneath),\n179-# damping = 0 (air drag). Pushing shares momentum: a 70 kg character barely moves 300 kg.\n180-# Reusable props made in the Object Studio replace shape and colour:\n181-#   asset = \"BUILTIN/bench\", scale = 1, body = \"fixed\" (or \"none\": no collision),\n182-#   seed = 3 (a variant: chance, jitter and pick; 0 as authored),\n183-#   roles = { \"$wall\" = \"#5a6b7c\" } (colours for the theme roles its parts name),\n184-#   patch = [{ op = \"scale\", by = 0.5 }] (asset_edit patch ops on this copy only: a one-off\n185-#   variant, such as a defect on show in rooms/limits.toml; publish variants rooms reuse).\n186-#   `room_check` names any asset the library does not have, or a patch that does not apply.\n187-# Visual-only effects on any object (never affect the simulation; body = \"none\" for invisible\n--\n276:# [[npc]]\n277-# name = \"spidey\"\n278-# kind = \"spider\"\n279-# pos = [6.5, 0, 4.5]\n280-# ai = { type = \"wander\", radius = 3 }\n281-# look = { accent = \"#3bb273\", leg_length = 1.0 }\n105:# prop = { ..., sway = \"leaves\" }   props (and [[object]]s) can sway: \"leaves\" | \"grass\"\n106-#\n107-# zone = { kind = \"...\", ... } makes the tile a trigger (identical neighbours merge):\n108-#   kind = \"start\" | \"finish\" | \"gate\" | \"checkpoint\" | \"kill\" | \"water\" | \"pad\" | \"camera\" |\n109-#          \"conveyor\" (facing = direction, speed = m/s; carries characters and props) |\n110-#          \"bounce\" (speed = launch m/s; trampolines for characters and props)\n111-#   course = \"name\"   start/finish/gates of one course share it; leaving START starts the timer,\n112-#                     gates must be passed in `index` order (missed gate = +2 s), FINISH stops it\n113-#   index = 1         gate order\n--\n138:[[object]]\n139-name = \"ball\"\n140-shape = { type = \"sphere\", radius = 0.4 }\n141-pos = [3.5, 1.0, 3.5]           # x = column, y = height, z = row\n142-color = \"#5b8def\"\n143-body = \"dynamic\"                # dynamic | fixed | kinematic | none\n144-\n145-# Animated objects use body = \"kinematic\" and a behavior (vectors are in the object's own frame):\n146-#   behavior = { type = \"move\", offset = [0, 0, 4], period = 4, phase = 0, hold = 0.3, smooth = true }\n87:[layout.legend.'.']\n88-blocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0, color = \"#c8c8c8\" }]\n89-\n90:[layout.legend.'#']\n91-blocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0, color = \"#c8c8c8\" }, { y0 = 0, y1 = 2.0, color = \"#9aa5b1\" }]\n92-\n93:[layout.legend.'B']\n94-blocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0, color = \"#c8c8c8\" }, { y0 = 0, y1 = 1.0, color = \"#c9a27a\", rounded = true }]\n95-# Other options: destructible = true, ghost = true (no collision), inset = 0.3 (thinner),\n96-# crumble = 0.8 (falls 0.8 s after being stepped on), regrow = 4 (comes back after 4 s),\n97-# strength = 40 (breaks when hit with more than this contact force, e.g. glass),\n98-# look = \"flat\" | \"cel\" | \"lit\" | \"unlit\",\n99-# ladder = { facing = \"north\", height = 3.0 },\n100-# prop = { shape = { type = \"box\", half = [0.35, 0.35, 0.35] }, color = \"#e8704a\" },\n101-# marker = \"player\"\natrium.toml\ncabin.toml\ncorridor.toml\ndepot.toml\nnightward.toml\noffice.toml\nrecovery.toml\nscrub.toml","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"staleReadFileStateHint":"[This command modified 2 files you've previously read: ../content.rs, ../field.rs. Call Read before editing.]"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BkWEDAqFyhMkq9u7MokNPP","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgjxij48iTE8mAXNDV3u6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0149ApRKX4vkJFLx88TryiWW","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-072416__x42677a/work/TraumaTempo-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-072416/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/content/story\nw() { cat > $1.toml; }\nw case0 <<'EOF'\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case0_before\"\nline = [\n { set = \"corridor\", music = \"tense\", cue = \"thunder\", flash = 0.6 },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"Port Verity. The storm has been coming for three days, and tonight it has arrived.\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"Mercy Harbor General. A public hospital, a teaching hospital, a hospital where half the wings have a benefactor's name and all of the roofs leak.\" },\n { enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"I'm a second-year. I've assisted. I have never, at any point, been the person the assisting was for.\" },\n { enter = \"bashir\", x = 3.1, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"Net-mender off Pier Nine. Hooks and cable splinters. The whole forearm, Doctor.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Where is Doctor Abara? Where is the attending?\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"The attending is elbow-deep in a bus driver. This one's yours, Doctor.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"My father tuned pianos. He could hear a flat string through a wall. He told me hands learn what ears already know.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"I don't know what that means, Bashir. I just thought someone should hear it, in case.\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"Scrub in, Doctor. His pulse is seventy-two. That is a good number. Start there.\" },\n { music = \"none\" },\n]\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case0_after\"\nline = [\n { set = \"scrub\", music = \"tender\", enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"soft\" },\n { enter = \"bashir\", x = 3.1, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"He will keep the arm. He has already asked whether we mend nets.\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"Your hands were steady.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"They weren't. I was counting his heartbeats.\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"Doctor.\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"It is a small word. He has fourteen ways of saying it. That was the third-kindest.\" },\n]\nEOF\nw case1 <<'EOF'\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case1_before\"\nline = [\n { set = \"office\", music = \"tense\", enter = \"voss\", x = 3.1, expr = \"stern\" },\n { enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Doctor Quill. You closed a forearm in a storm and the patient tells my nurses you are an angel.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"Thank you, Chief. I...\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"That was not a compliment. In my hospital, adequate is a kind of malpractice, and angels are worse. Angels do not chart.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"This morning you have a harbour pilot with an appendix. A routine appendix. I will be in the gallery.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"You'll be watching a routine appendix?\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"There are no routine appendixes, Doctor. There are only surgeons who have not yet been surprised.\" },\n { camera = \"or_wide\", set = \"office\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"Operating Theatre Two. Rosalind Pike, who has brought nine thousand ships past the Verity Shoals, counts backward from ten and reaches seven.\" },\n { camera = \"paper\" },\n]\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case1_after\"\nline = [\n { set = \"scrub\", music = \"tender\", enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { enter = \"voss\", x = 3.1, expr = \"stern\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"The artery. It shouldn't have, there was no reason it should have let go. I checked the ligature, I...\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Adequate.\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"Chief Ottoline Voss left the scrub room. Nurses later reported that she had used the word without visible pain.\" },\n { enter = \"teddy\", x = 0.0, expr = \"soft\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"That's the nicest thing she's said since the Millennium. I think she's in love with you. I'm so sorry.\" },\n]\nEOF\nw case2 <<'EOF'\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case2_before\"\nline = [\n { set = \"corridor\", music = \"tense\", cue = \"thunder\", flash = 1.0, shake = 1.0, enter = \"teddy\", x = 3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"11:40 p.m. Grain Terminal Four goes up with a sound they will hear in the next county.\" },\n { enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"We have nineteen in the corridor and two working monitors, and one of them is displaying the weather. It's accurate. I checked.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Who's the worst?\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"The foreman. He walked out carrying a man and then sat down and said he felt a bit odd. He has a bolt in him, Mara. Possibly a lot of bolts.\" },\n { enter = \"bashir\", x = 0.0, expr = \"stern\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Table's ready, Doctor. Teddy, breathe. Through the nose. Not the patient's nose.\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"I'm fine. I joke when I'm scared. That's why you've never heard me not joking.\" },\n]\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case2_after\"\nline = [\n { set = \"recovery\", music = \"tender\", enter = \"bashir\", x = 3.1, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"He'll live. Everyone keeps telling me I did well. Teddy keeps telling me I did something strange.\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"You said now.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"I'm sorry?\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"You said 'now,' Doctor. Half a beat before the monitor flatlined. Before the alarm. Before anything in that room could have told you.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"I, it went flat. Inside. Like a string going slack. I can't...\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"I am not asking anything, Doctor.\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"I wanted you to know that I am not asking.\" },\n]\nEOF\nw case3 <<'EOF'\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case3_before\"\nline = [\n { set = \"atrium\", music = \"tender\", enter = \"vane\", x = 3.1, expr = \"soft\" },\n { enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"The Vane Wing. Forty million in new surgical suites, one string quartet, and a canape that no one is able to identify.\" },\n { who = \"vane\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"You must be the young woman from the terminal fire. No, don't be embarrassed. Doctor Quill, isn't it? Everyone is talking.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Ms. Vane. I didn't, they told me to come in my good coat. This is it. This is my good coat.\" },\n { who = \"vane\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"Cordelia. Please. It's a lovely coat. My mother was a nurse, you know, on this very harbour. All of this is only a very long thank-you note.\" },\n { who = \"vane\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"The city needs hands like yours, Doctor. Steady ones. You have my card, should the Foundation ever be able to help.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"That's so kind. Nobody has ever said anything kind to me in this building.\" },\n { exit = \"vane\", enter = \"bashir\", x = 3.1, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"Doctor. A courier from the Foundation's own office. Benign liver mass, scheduled. Theatre Six is free, and the Chief asks that it be quick.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"Benign. Scheduled. Quick. Bashir, tonight might be the first normal night of my life.\" },\n]\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case3_after\"\nline = [\n { set = \"nightward\", music = \"tense\", enter = \"voss\", x = 3.1, expr = \"stern\" },\n { enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { enter = \"bashir\", x = 0.0, expr = \"stern\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"It split. It stepped. It kept time, Chief. In three. I felt the whole room go quiet, and then everything was so slow, and my hands...\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Theatre Six has been sealed for a gas leak. The logs for tonight show a routine excision.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"There's no gas leak.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"You will wash your hands, you will sign nothing, and you will tell no one what you did not see in this room.\" },\n]\nEOF\nw case4 <<'EOF'\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case4_before\"\nline = [\n { set = \"nightward\", music = \"tense\", enter = \"voss\", x = 3.1, expr = \"stern\", cue = \"lift\" },\n { enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"Below the morgue level there is a lift that stops at a floor with no button. The floor has no name on any plan. The staff call it the Night Ward.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"How long has this been here?\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"Eleven years. Sit down, Doctor. You have met a thing tonight, and it deserves its full name.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"We call it Requiem. Recombinant Enzymatic Quiescent Immuno-Evasive Microfilaria. It is the only organism ever designed to keep time.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Keep time for what?\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"For the end of you, Doctor.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"It entrains to the host's heartbeat, then it conducts. Introit, the first movement, you met in a liver. Each strain has a meter. Each has an appetite.\" },\n { enter = \"teddy\", x = 0.0, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Chief. Sorry, Chief. Sorry, is this, are we allowed down here? The pilot's back. Rosalind Pike. She came in for a cough.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Seeded during recovery. On my ward. In my hospital.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"I have no guidance to give you, Doctor Quill. No one has ever finished this operation. Scrub.\" },\n]\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case4_after\"\nline = [\n { set = \"nightward\", music = \"tender\", enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"soft\" },\n { enter = \"teddy\", x = 3.1, expr = \"soft\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"She's asking for her boat. She's asking whose idea the lung was. Mara, you did it. Nobody's ever... Mara?\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Teddy. I can't open my hands.\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"Both hands had closed around instruments no longer in them. Then her knees, without consulting anyone, resigned.\" },\n { exit = \"mara\", shake = 1.0, cue = \"gasp\" },\n { enter = \"voss\", x = -3.1, expr = \"stern\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Three days' rest, and she will need three weeks. The strains won't wait three days.\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Then what do we do? Who else is there? Who else could possibly...\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"There is one surgeon in this city who has seen worse than this and said so, loudly, in front of the board.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Then we need a second opinion.\" },\n]\nEOF\nw case5 <<'EOF'\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case5_before\"\nline = [\n { set = \"depot\", music = \"tender\", cue = \"thunder\", enter = \"pet\", x = 3.1, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"The Harbour Road bus depot, 3 a.m. A tea machine that the transit authority has twice attempted to condemn.\" },\n { enter = \"teddy\", x = -3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Doctor Nwosu? Doctor Perpetua Nwosu? Chief Voss sent me. I've read your paper on crush injuries. I've read it several times. I cried, once, at the tables.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"This tea is the colour of a bruise on day five, young man, and it is the most honest thing that has happened to me since I retired.\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"She says you're the only one left who can do it. She said to say please.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Ottoline Voss has not said please since the Berlin Wall. Hold this.\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"She handed him the cup. It was only then, as he took it, that he saw the tea was shivering, and that the cup was not what was shaking it.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"You saw that. Good. You'll not mention it. Thirty years ago these hands could stitch a mayfly. Now they stitch whatever is nearest.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"What have you got for me?\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"A longshoreman with a shattered femur. It's, the femur's a warm-up. Sorry. It's a test. She said you'd know.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Of course it's a test. Let's see if they still let me fail.\" },\n]\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case5_after\"\nline = [\n { set = \"scrub\", music = \"tense\", enter = \"pet\", x = -3.1, expr = \"stern\" },\n { enter = \"voss\", x = 3.1, expr = \"stern\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Your right hand shakes, Perpetua.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Your right hand signs the budget, Ottoline. We've all got our tremors.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"There were two sets of hands on that field. I have seen the footage. I am not going to ask.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"Thirty-three years, and you pick tonight to start not asking. You look terrible. You look like the inside of a...\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"I am quite all right. I merely need to sit for a...\" },\n { exit = \"voss\", shake = 1.0, cue = \"gasp\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Ottoline.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Somebody get a table. And somebody tell me why the Chief of Surgery has a fever of forty-one in a time signature.\" },\n]\nEOF\nw case6 <<'EOF'\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case6_before\"\nline = [\n { set = \"nightward\", music = \"tense\", enter = \"voss\", x = 3.1, expr = \"soft\" },\n { enter = \"pet\", x = -3.1, expr = \"stern\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"Eleven years. It's in the pericardium. The strain is Dies Irae: it runs hot. I have been keeping it down with ice baths and contempt.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Eleven years? How does a person catch a designed parasite eleven years before anyone else?\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"One doesn't catch it, Perpetua. One injects it. It is what careful people do with the first dose.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"You built it.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"I built the clock. A cure for arrhythmia, a tiny metronome that lives in the blood. Someone very generous paid for my lab. Someone very generous asked what else it could conduct.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"I built the Night Ward to bury what I made. It has taken longer than I expected.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"I ought to leave you on this table.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"Yes. You should scrub first, though. It's only hygienic.\" },\n]\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case6_after\"\nline = [\n { set = \"recovery\", music = \"tender\", enter = \"voss\", x = 3.1, expr = \"soft\" },\n { enter = \"pet\", x = -3.1, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"Your closure is uneven at the third stitch.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"Your face is uneven at the third stitch. Who paid for it, Ottoline? Say the name, or I'll put it all back.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Her mother was a nurse. On this very harbour. She tells everyone.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Cordelia Vane.\" },\n { set = \"corridor\", music = \"tender\", enter = \"bashir\", x = 0.0, expr = \"soft\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"That same morning a card arrives for the surgical staff, in a warm and generous hand, with an arrangement of white lilies the size of a child.\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"'To the steadiest hands in Port Verity. With a very long thank-you.' How thoughtful. I'll put them in water.\" },\n]\nEOF\nw case7 <<'EOF'\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case7_before\"\nline = [\n { set = \"corridor\", music = \"tense\", enter = \"teddy\", x = 3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { enter = \"pet\", x = -3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"He was changing the water. He said, 'Doctor,' just like that, to nobody, and then he sat down on the floor. Pet. He's in four-four and then he isn't.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"The flowers. Every strain at once, in the pollen. She's sent us the whole Mass in a vase.\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"He's the one who, he talks everyone through it. He talks me through breakfast. Who's going to say 'Doctor'?\" },\n { set = \"nightward\", enter = \"pet\", x = -3.1, expr = \"stern\" },\n { enter = \"teddy\", x = 3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { enter = \"mara\", x = 0.0, expr = \"stern\", cue = \"lift\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"I can hear him from the lift. He's flat. All of him.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"You. You should be on your back with your hands in plaster, girl. I've read your chart.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"My hands hurt, Doctor Nwosu. They hurt in tune. I think I can do this if somebody keeps the other half.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"I have buried better surgeons than you.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"I'd like not to do it tonight. Take the right. I'll take the left.\" },\n { camera = \"or_wide\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"The Night Ward. Two surgeons. One table. A silence where a voice has been, every night, for all of this.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Scalpel.\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"Nobody hands it to her.\" },\n { camera = \"paper\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"...I'll do it. I've seen it done. Mostly.\" },\n]\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case7_after\"\nline = [\n { set = \"recovery\", music = \"tender\", enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"soft\" },\n { enter = \"pet\", x = 3.1, expr = \"soft\" },\n { enter = \"bashir\", x = 0.0, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"Seven o'clock. It has, against all custom, stopped raining.\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"Your closure.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Bashir. You're awake. You shouldn't, don't try to...\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"Clean, Doctor.\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"That was the kindest. There turn out to be fifteen.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"I'm told this city has a vacancy for a terrible old woman. I'm told there's tea.\" },\n { set = \"cabin\", music = \"tense\", cue = \"phone\", enter = \"vane\", x = 0.0, expr = \"soft\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"Elsewhere. A very good ship, in very deep water, with a very long view.\" },\n { who = \"vane\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"Yes. I saw. Two of them, wasn't it? And such steady hands. No, darling, don't apologise. It was never about the one city.\" },\n { who = \"vane\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"A promising first movement. Have them tune the orchestra.\" },\n { flash = 0.4 },\n]\nEOF\ncd .. ; cat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Making more of the game: the designer guide\n\nEverything here is a text file. Native builds read them from disk: edit, reload the case (or use\nthe dev panel's *Reload content*), no rebuild. `pav case_check path=<file>` checks one file and names\nthe line of any error; `cargo test -p pav_core --test surgery` lints all of them. **A new file must\nalso be listed in `FILES` in `../content.rs`**; a test fails if one is missing.\n\n## Add a case\nCopy `cases/case0.toml`, list it in `FILES`, and give it a slot in `load()`.\n- `surgeon`, `plate`, `timer` (s), `par` (the score for rank S; `pav balance` suggests one), `patient`, `life`,\n  `diagnosis`, `fate` (the line on the results screen), `before`/`after` (story scene ids), `gift`\n  (`none`, `hush`, `echo`, `duet`), `gift_locked`, `music`, `ring` (8 instruments, clockwise from up).\n- Each `[[phase]]`: `now` (the NOW line), `guide` (highlights targets), `checkpoint` (retry here), `spawn`, `say`\n  (`{who, text, at}`), `strain` + `params`, `meter` (ECG beats to the bar), `reveal_plate` (crossfades from the cut),\n  `code_shocks` (a scripted stop), `banner`, `linger`.\n- A phase ends when its blocking hazards and strain are done. `[[phase.trigger]]` adds a twist: `at_time`,\n  `vitals_below`, `on_clear`, `on_beat`, then `spawn`, `say`, `cue`, `banner`, `gift_full`, `vitals_hit`.\n- Spawn kinds: `incision` (a b c) · `closure` · `lacer` (a b) · `bleeder` (a ang) · `pool` (a r) · `object` (a ang sub:\n  0 hook 1 shard 2 splinter; `hidden`) · `polyp` · `tumor` (a r ang) · `patch` · `burn` · `bone` (a b ang). `optional = true`\n  doesn't hold the phase open. x runs -9..9 and z -4..4.2; angles are degrees.\n\n## Add a strain\nA strain is a state machine in `../strain.rs`: add a `StrainKind`, a `start_strain` arm and a tick. It reads the heart's\n`r_wave` and spends `beat_worth` per beat, so its speed-up is clamped for you. Teach the bot (`../bot.rs`), then add\nthe name to `STRAINS` in `content.rs` and to `cover.rs`.\n\n## Add a line of dialogue\nIn `story/*.toml`, a scene is a list of `line`s, played in order: `{ who, expr, text }`, or a stage command\n`set`, `enter` + `x`, `exit`, `music`, `cue`, `camera` (`paper`, `or_wide`), `flash`, `shake`. Commands can share a line\nwith text. `who = \"narrator\"` is a caption with no speaker. In-op barks live in `callouts.toml`.\n\n## Add a character\nCopy `rigs/bashir.toml`. `[colors]` names colours for the shared parts in `_face.toml` (`skin shade blush scrubs iris\nbrow`). `[[part]]` adds hair and accessories: `z` is the layer (a new layer draws an ink line), `points` a closed outline, `chaikin`\nhow many times to round it, `layer` what moves it (`head`, `hair`, `eyes`, `brow`, `lid`). `[expr.*]` needs at least `neutral`,\n`alarmed`, `stern`, `soft`. `[voice]` sets the gibberish: `base` pitch, `wave`, `speed`, `jitter`, `bright`.\n\n## Add a plate or set\n`plates/*.toml`: `lobes` (ellipses raising the tissue), `vessels`, four colours, `pulse`, `noise`, `veins`, `bone`.\n`sets/*.toml`: `card`s (`rect` or `points`, `z` for parallax, `emissive`, `blink`), `rain`, `lamp`, `back`.\nEOF\ncd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-072416__x42677a/work/TraumaTempo-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-072416/engine; grep -n \"npc\\|object\" rooms/_template.toml | head -20; sed -n '/^\\[\\[npc\\]\\]/,/^$/p' rooms/_template.toml | head -30; CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=6 cargo check --locked -p pav_core 2>&1 | grep -E \"^(error|warning: unused)|^  -->\" -A6 | head -120","description":"Write the story script and designer guide, then check pav_core","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23652,"cache_read_input_tokens":343869,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23652},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"189b0832-eeab-4401-af9a-06d1cd0033c9","uuid":"98f4873a-5a08-4046-81c7-4986f950adb6","timestamp":"2026-11-05T14:47:58.195Z","request_id":"req_011CgjxiihobxtKCqyJkkuQk","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0149ApRKX4vkJFLx88TryiWW":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-072416__x42677a/work/TraumaTempo-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-072416/engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/surgery/content/story\nw() { cat > $1.toml; }\nw case0 <<'EOF'\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case0_before\"\nline = [\n { set = \"corridor\", music = \"tense\", cue = \"thunder\", flash = 0.6 },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"Port Verity. The storm has been coming for three days, and tonight it has arrived.\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"Mercy Harbor General. A public hospital, a teaching hospital, a hospital where half the wings have a benefactor's name and all of the roofs leak.\" },\n { enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"I'm a second-year. I've assisted. I have never, at any point, been the person the assisting was for.\" },\n { enter = \"bashir\", x = 3.1, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"Net-mender off Pier Nine. Hooks and cable splinters. The whole forearm, Doctor.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Where is Doctor Abara? Where is the attending?\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"The attending is elbow-deep in a bus driver. This one's yours, Doctor.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"My father tuned pianos. He could hear a flat string through a wall. He told me hands learn what ears already know.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"I don't know what that means, Bashir. I just thought someone should hear it, in case.\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"Scrub in, Doctor. His pulse is seventy-two. That is a good number. Start there.\" },\n { music = \"none\" },\n]\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case0_after\"\nline = [\n { set = \"scrub\", music = \"tender\", enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"soft\" },\n { enter = \"bashir\", x = 3.1, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"He will keep the arm. He has already asked whether we mend nets.\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"Your hands were steady.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"They weren't. I was counting his heartbeats.\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"Doctor.\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"It is a small word. He has fourteen ways of saying it. That was the third-kindest.\" },\n]\nEOF\nw case1 <<'EOF'\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case1_before\"\nline = [\n { set = \"office\", music = \"tense\", enter = \"voss\", x = 3.1, expr = \"stern\" },\n { enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Doctor Quill. You closed a forearm in a storm and the patient tells my nurses you are an angel.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"Thank you, Chief. I...\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"That was not a compliment. In my hospital, adequate is a kind of malpractice, and angels are worse. Angels do not chart.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"This morning you have a harbour pilot with an appendix. A routine appendix. I will be in the gallery.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"You'll be watching a routine appendix?\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"There are no routine appendixes, Doctor. There are only surgeons who have not yet been surprised.\" },\n { camera = \"or_wide\", set = \"office\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"Operating Theatre Two. Rosalind Pike, who has brought nine thousand ships past the Verity Shoals, counts backward from ten and reaches seven.\" },\n { camera = \"paper\" },\n]\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case1_after\"\nline = [\n { set = \"scrub\", music = \"tender\", enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { enter = \"voss\", x = 3.1, expr = \"stern\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"The artery. It shouldn't have, there was no reason it should have let go. I checked the ligature, I...\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Adequate.\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"Chief Ottoline Voss left the scrub room. Nurses later reported that she had used the word without visible pain.\" },\n { enter = \"teddy\", x = 0.0, expr = \"soft\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"That's the nicest thing she's said since the Millennium. I think she's in love with you. I'm so sorry.\" },\n]\nEOF\nw case2 <<'EOF'\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case2_before\"\nline = [\n { set = \"corridor\", music = \"tense\", cue = \"thunder\", flash = 1.0, shake = 1.0, enter = \"teddy\", x = 3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"11:40 p.m. Grain Terminal Four goes up with a sound they will hear in the next county.\" },\n { enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"We have nineteen in the corridor and two working monitors, and one of them is displaying the weather. It's accurate. I checked.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Who's the worst?\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"The foreman. He walked out carrying a man and then sat down and said he felt a bit odd. He has a bolt in him, Mara. Possibly a lot of bolts.\" },\n { enter = \"bashir\", x = 0.0, expr = \"stern\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Table's ready, Doctor. Teddy, breathe. Through the nose. Not the patient's nose.\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"I'm fine. I joke when I'm scared. That's why you've never heard me not joking.\" },\n]\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case2_after\"\nline = [\n { set = \"recovery\", music = \"tender\", enter = \"bashir\", x = 3.1, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"He'll live. Everyone keeps telling me I did well. Teddy keeps telling me I did something strange.\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"You said now.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"I'm sorry?\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"You said 'now,' Doctor. Half a beat before the monitor flatlined. Before the alarm. Before anything in that room could have told you.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"I, it went flat. Inside. Like a string going slack. I can't...\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"I am not asking anything, Doctor.\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"I wanted you to know that I am not asking.\" },\n]\nEOF\nw case3 <<'EOF'\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case3_before\"\nline = [\n { set = \"atrium\", music = \"tender\", enter = \"vane\", x = 3.1, expr = \"soft\" },\n { enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"The Vane Wing. Forty million in new surgical suites, one string quartet, and a canape that no one is able to identify.\" },\n { who = \"vane\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"You must be the young woman from the terminal fire. No, don't be embarrassed. Doctor Quill, isn't it? Everyone is talking.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Ms. Vane. I didn't, they told me to come in my good coat. This is it. This is my good coat.\" },\n { who = \"vane\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"Cordelia. Please. It's a lovely coat. My mother was a nurse, you know, on this very harbour. All of this is only a very long thank-you note.\" },\n { who = \"vane\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"The city needs hands like yours, Doctor. Steady ones. You have my card, should the Foundation ever be able to help.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"That's so kind. Nobody has ever said anything kind to me in this building.\" },\n { exit = \"vane\", enter = \"bashir\", x = 3.1, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"Doctor. A courier from the Foundation's own office. Benign liver mass, scheduled. Theatre Six is free, and the Chief asks that it be quick.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"Benign. Scheduled. Quick. Bashir, tonight might be the first normal night of my life.\" },\n]\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case3_after\"\nline = [\n { set = \"nightward\", music = \"tense\", enter = \"voss\", x = 3.1, expr = \"stern\" },\n { enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { enter = \"bashir\", x = 0.0, expr = \"stern\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"It split. It stepped. It kept time, Chief. In three. I felt the whole room go quiet, and then everything was so slow, and my hands...\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Theatre Six has been sealed for a gas leak. The logs for tonight show a routine excision.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"There's no gas leak.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"You will wash your hands, you will sign nothing, and you will tell no one what you did not see in this room.\" },\n]\nEOF\nw case4 <<'EOF'\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case4_before\"\nline = [\n { set = \"nightward\", music = \"tense\", enter = \"voss\", x = 3.1, expr = \"stern\", cue = \"lift\" },\n { enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"Below the morgue level there is a lift that stops at a floor with no button. The floor has no name on any plan. The staff call it the Night Ward.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"How long has this been here?\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"Eleven years. Sit down, Doctor. You have met a thing tonight, and it deserves its full name.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"We call it Requiem. Recombinant Enzymatic Quiescent Immuno-Evasive Microfilaria. It is the only organism ever designed to keep time.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Keep time for what?\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"For the end of you, Doctor.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"It entrains to the host's heartbeat, then it conducts. Introit, the first movement, you met in a liver. Each strain has a meter. Each has an appetite.\" },\n { enter = \"teddy\", x = 0.0, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Chief. Sorry, Chief. Sorry, is this, are we allowed down here? The pilot's back. Rosalind Pike. She came in for a cough.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Seeded during recovery. On my ward. In my hospital.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"I have no guidance to give you, Doctor Quill. No one has ever finished this operation. Scrub.\" },\n]\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case4_after\"\nline = [\n { set = \"nightward\", music = \"tender\", enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"soft\" },\n { enter = \"teddy\", x = 3.1, expr = \"soft\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"She's asking for her boat. She's asking whose idea the lung was. Mara, you did it. Nobody's ever... Mara?\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Teddy. I can't open my hands.\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"Both hands had closed around instruments no longer in them. Then her knees, without consulting anyone, resigned.\" },\n { exit = \"mara\", shake = 1.0, cue = \"gasp\" },\n { enter = \"voss\", x = -3.1, expr = \"stern\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Three days' rest, and she will need three weeks. The strains won't wait three days.\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Then what do we do? Who else is there? Who else could possibly...\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"There is one surgeon in this city who has seen worse than this and said so, loudly, in front of the board.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Then we need a second opinion.\" },\n]\nEOF\nw case5 <<'EOF'\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case5_before\"\nline = [\n { set = \"depot\", music = \"tender\", cue = \"thunder\", enter = \"pet\", x = 3.1, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"The Harbour Road bus depot, 3 a.m. A tea machine that the transit authority has twice attempted to condemn.\" },\n { enter = \"teddy\", x = -3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Doctor Nwosu? Doctor Perpetua Nwosu? Chief Voss sent me. I've read your paper on crush injuries. I've read it several times. I cried, once, at the tables.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"This tea is the colour of a bruise on day five, young man, and it is the most honest thing that has happened to me since I retired.\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"She says you're the only one left who can do it. She said to say please.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Ottoline Voss has not said please since the Berlin Wall. Hold this.\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"She handed him the cup. It was only then, as he took it, that he saw the tea was shivering, and that the cup was not what was shaking it.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"You saw that. Good. You'll not mention it. Thirty years ago these hands could stitch a mayfly. Now they stitch whatever is nearest.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"What have you got for me?\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"A longshoreman with a shattered femur. It's, the femur's a warm-up. Sorry. It's a test. She said you'd know.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Of course it's a test. Let's see if they still let me fail.\" },\n]\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case5_after\"\nline = [\n { set = \"scrub\", music = \"tense\", enter = \"pet\", x = -3.1, expr = \"stern\" },\n { enter = \"voss\", x = 3.1, expr = \"stern\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Your right hand shakes, Perpetua.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Your right hand signs the budget, Ottoline. We've all got our tremors.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"There were two sets of hands on that field. I have seen the footage. I am not going to ask.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"Thirty-three years, and you pick tonight to start not asking. You look terrible. You look like the inside of a...\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"I am quite all right. I merely need to sit for a...\" },\n { exit = \"voss\", shake = 1.0, cue = \"gasp\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Ottoline.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Somebody get a table. And somebody tell me why the Chief of Surgery has a fever of forty-one in a time signature.\" },\n]\nEOF\nw case6 <<'EOF'\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case6_before\"\nline = [\n { set = \"nightward\", music = \"tense\", enter = \"voss\", x = 3.1, expr = \"soft\" },\n { enter = \"pet\", x = -3.1, expr = \"stern\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"Eleven years. It's in the pericardium. The strain is Dies Irae: it runs hot. I have been keeping it down with ice baths and contempt.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Eleven years? How does a person catch a designed parasite eleven years before anyone else?\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"One doesn't catch it, Perpetua. One injects it. It is what careful people do with the first dose.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"You built it.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"I built the clock. A cure for arrhythmia, a tiny metronome that lives in the blood. Someone very generous paid for my lab. Someone very generous asked what else it could conduct.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"I built the Night Ward to bury what I made. It has taken longer than I expected.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"I ought to leave you on this table.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"Yes. You should scrub first, though. It's only hygienic.\" },\n]\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case6_after\"\nline = [\n { set = \"recovery\", music = \"tender\", enter = \"voss\", x = 3.1, expr = \"soft\" },\n { enter = \"pet\", x = -3.1, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"Your closure is uneven at the third stitch.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"Your face is uneven at the third stitch. Who paid for it, Ottoline? Say the name, or I'll put it all back.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Her mother was a nurse. On this very harbour. She tells everyone.\" },\n { who = \"voss\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Cordelia Vane.\" },\n { set = \"corridor\", music = \"tender\", enter = \"bashir\", x = 0.0, expr = \"soft\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"That same morning a card arrives for the surgical staff, in a warm and generous hand, with an arrangement of white lilies the size of a child.\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"'To the steadiest hands in Port Verity. With a very long thank-you.' How thoughtful. I'll put them in water.\" },\n]\nEOF\nw case7 <<'EOF'\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case7_before\"\nline = [\n { set = \"corridor\", music = \"tense\", enter = \"teddy\", x = 3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { enter = \"pet\", x = -3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"He was changing the water. He said, 'Doctor,' just like that, to nobody, and then he sat down on the floor. Pet. He's in four-four and then he isn't.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"The flowers. Every strain at once, in the pollen. She's sent us the whole Mass in a vase.\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"He's the one who, he talks everyone through it. He talks me through breakfast. Who's going to say 'Doctor'?\" },\n { set = \"nightward\", enter = \"pet\", x = -3.1, expr = \"stern\" },\n { enter = \"teddy\", x = 3.1, expr = \"alarmed\" },\n { enter = \"mara\", x = 0.0, expr = \"stern\", cue = \"lift\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"I can hear him from the lift. He's flat. All of him.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"You. You should be on your back with your hands in plaster, girl. I've read your chart.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"My hands hurt, Doctor Nwosu. They hurt in tune. I think I can do this if somebody keeps the other half.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"I have buried better surgeons than you.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"I'd like not to do it tonight. Take the right. I'll take the left.\" },\n { camera = \"or_wide\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"The Night Ward. Two surgeons. One table. A silence where a voice has been, every night, for all of this.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"stern\", text = \"Scalpel.\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"Nobody hands it to her.\" },\n { camera = \"paper\" },\n { who = \"teddy\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"...I'll do it. I've seen it done. Mostly.\" },\n]\n[[scene]]\nid = \"case7_after\"\nline = [\n { set = \"recovery\", music = \"tender\", enter = \"mara\", x = -3.1, expr = \"soft\" },\n { enter = \"pet\", x = 3.1, expr = \"soft\" },\n { enter = \"bashir\", x = 0.0, expr = \"neutral\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"Seven o'clock. It has, against all custom, stopped raining.\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"neutral\", text = \"Your closure.\" },\n { who = \"mara\", expr = \"alarmed\", text = \"Bashir. You're awake. You shouldn't, don't try to...\" },\n { who = \"bashir\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"Clean, Doctor.\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"That was the kindest. There turn out to be fifteen.\" },\n { who = \"pet\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"I'm told this city has a vacancy for a terrible old woman. I'm told there's tea.\" },\n { set = \"cabin\", music = \"tense\", cue = \"phone\", enter = \"vane\", x = 0.0, expr = \"soft\" },\n { who = \"narrator\", text = \"Elsewhere. A very good ship, in very deep water, with a very long view.\" },\n { who = \"vane\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"Yes. I saw. Two of them, wasn't it? And such steady hands. No, darling, don't apologise. It was never about the one city.\" },\n { who = \"vane\", expr = \"soft\", text = \"A promising first movement. Have them tune the orchestra.\" },\n { flash = 0.4 },\n]\nEOF\ncd .. ; cat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# Making more of the game: the designer guide\n\nEverything here is a text file. Native builds read them from disk: edit, reload the case (or use\nthe dev panel's *Reload content*), no rebuild. `pav case_check path=<file>` checks one file and names\nthe line of any error; `cargo test -p pav_core --test surgery` lints all of them. **A new file must\nalso be listed in `FILES` in `../content.rs`**; a test fails if one is missing.\n\n## Add a case\nCopy `cases/case0.toml`, list it in `FILES`, and give it a slot in `load()`.\n- `surgeon`, `plate`, `timer` (s), `par` (the score for rank S; `pav balance` suggests one), `patient`, `life`,\n  `diagnosis`, `fate` (the line on the results screen), `before`/`after` (story scene ids), `gift`\n  (`none`, `hush`, `echo`, `duet`), `gift_locked`, `music`, `ring` (8 instruments, clockwise from up).\n- Each `[[phase]]`: `now` (the NOW line), `guide` (highlights targets), `checkpoint` (retry here), `spawn`, `say`\n  (`{who, text, at}`), `strain` + `params`, `meter` (ECG beats to the bar), `reveal_plate` (crossfades from the cut),\n  `code_shocks` (a scripted stop), `banner`, `linger`.\n- A phase ends when its blocking hazards and strain are done. `[[phase.trigger]]` adds a twist: `at_time`,\n  `vitals_below`, `on_clear`, `on_beat`, then `spawn`, `say`, `cue`, `banner`, `gift_full`, `vitals_hit`.\n- Spawn kinds: `incision` (a b c) · `closure` · `lacer` (a b) · `bleeder` (a ang) · `pool` (a r) · `object` (a ang sub:\n  0 hook 1 shard 2 splinter; `hidden`) · `polyp` · `tumor` (a r ang) · `patch` · `burn` · `bone` (a b ang). `optional = true`\n  doesn't hold the phase open. x runs -9..9 and z -4..4.2; angles are degrees.\n\n## Add a strain\nA strain is a state machine in `../strain.rs`: add a `StrainKind`, a `start_strain` arm and a tick. It reads the heart's\n`r_wave` and spends `beat_worth` per beat, so its speed-up is clamped for you. Teach the bot (`../bot.rs`), then add\nthe name to `STRAINS` in `content.rs` and to `cover.rs`.\n\n## Add a line of dialogue\nIn `story/*.toml`, a scene is a list of `line`s, played in order: `{ who, expr, text }`, or a stage command\n`set`, `enter` + `x`, `exit`, `music`, `cue`, `camera` (`paper`, `or_wide`), `flash`, `shake`. Commands can share a line\nwith text. `who = \"narrator\"` is a caption with no speaker. In-op barks live in `callouts.toml`.\n\n## Add a character\nCopy `rigs/bashir.toml`. `[colors]` names colours for the shared parts in `_face.toml` (`skin shade blush scrubs iris\nbrow`). `[[part]]` adds hair and accessories: `z` is the layer (a new layer draws an ink line), `points` a closed outline, `chaikin`\nhow many times to round it, `layer` what moves it (`head`, `hair`, `eyes`, `brow`, `lid`). `[expr.*]` needs at least `neutral`,\n`alarmed`, `stern`, `soft`. `[voice]` sets the gibberish: `base` pitch, `wave`, `speed`, `jitter`, `bright`.\n\n## Add a plate or set\n`plates/*.toml`: `lobes` (ellipses raising the tissue), `vessels`, four colours, `pulse`, `noise`, `veins`, `bone`.\n`sets/*.toml`: `card`s (`rect` or `points`, `z` for parallax, `emissive`, `blink`), `rain`, `lamp`, `back`.\nEOF\ncd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-072416__x42677a/work/TraumaTempo-TraumaCenterSecondOpinion-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-072416/engine; grep -n \"npc\\|object\" rooms/_template.toml | head -20; sed -n '/^\\[\\[npc\\]\\]/,/^$/p' rooms/_template.toml | head -30; CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=6 cargo check --locked -p pav_core 2>&1 | grep -E \"^(error|warning: unused)|^  -->\" -A6 | head -120","description":"Write the story script and designer guide, then check pav_core","timeout":300000}}}
